! mcp_bootstrap_p131.strap -- "STANDARD FIXUPS", printed page 131.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.138, header READ and not assumed:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID ED000001   DIST. OF
! 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  131".
!
! >>> THE HEADER'S "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK ON THIS PAGE. <<<
! printed p.128 prints "LOCATION 216240" there and this deck's
! predecessor used it as a second reading of the first word.  Here
! the field is empty -- rendered at 600 dpi beside p.128's for the
! comparison -- and the reason is visible on the page: line 1 is a
! COMMENT CARD, so the page's first card has no location to print.
! The origin below therefore rests on line 4's SLC and line 5, not
! on the header.
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE. <<<  The card-serial column
! runs ED000001 (line 1) to ED000048 (line 48) -- forty-eight
! consecutive serials for forty-eight lines, ONE CARD PER LINE, no
! semicolon double-statement cards.  Counted off the serial column,
! nothing fell off the top or the bottom of the render.  printed
! p.128 was punching EB0003xx.
!
! FORTY-EIGHT LINES.  Lines 1-3 are a comment banner and line 28's
! CNOP compiles nothing, so FORTY-FOUR rows carry a LOCATION.  The
! page runs 216373.40 (line 4) .. 216440.00 (line 48).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BACKWARD JOIN IS WITNESSED BY THE PAGE ITSELF
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 4 PRINTS "SLC,$" AT 216373.40. <<<  An SLC emits nothing,
! so its printed LOCATION *is* the counter arriving from printed
! p.130 -- a free, independent reading of the join, printed by IBM's
! own assembler (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A PRINTED SLC,$ IS
! THE BEST FORWARD-JOIN WITNESS THERE IS").  p.130 is not
! transcribed, so this deck writes the hard origin "SLC,(8)216373.40"
! and ASSERTS what the page CHECKS; the printed card is recorded here
! and in line 4's note so that the witness is not thrown away.
!
! The volume OCR of printed p.130 agrees: its line 53 reads
! "216373.00  217372.10 00  B,SVISP" (docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt
! line 6832) -- a half word at 216373.00 leaves the counter at
! 216373.40, exactly where this page's SLC lands.  Its line 54 is a
! SYN ("215166.00+ ... SINTE SYN,WINTOR"), which spends no storage.
! THAT IS AN OCR READING, NOT A RENDERED ONE; when p.130 lands,
! compare by hand.
!
! Line 5's CNOP is the proof that the counter really arrived on a
! HALF word: a CNOP emits a NOP only when the counter is odd, and
! this one prints "000000.30 00" at 216373.40 while line 28's CNOP,
! reached at the full word 216412.00, prints NOTHING AT ALL -- no
! location, no binary.  Two CNOPs on one page, one firing and one
! not, is the page's own demonstration of the rule.
!
! THE FORWARD JOIN: the counter leaves line 47 at 216440.00, which
! is line 48's printed LOCATION, and printed p.132 line 1 is at
! 216440.40 (volume OCR).  See "LINE 48 IS NOT IN THIS DECK" below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Ten "standard fixup" entry points, laid out as a table, plus the
! commentator call they all funnel into.
!
! Lines 6-20   FIVE fixups that go to YMFL.  Each is three cards:
!              "SIC,YMFL / B,YMFL / (IQSX)DD(BU),<name>X".  The SIC
!              and the branch are ONE 64-bit instruction (Reference
!              Manual printed p.41), and the DD after them is a
!              four-character-wide IQS literal naming the fixup:
!              MK, IK, IJ, EK, CPUS.  The names match the labels --
!              YFXMK/MK, YFXIK/IK, YFXIJ/IJ, YFXEK/EK, YFXCPU/CPUS.
! Lines 21-28  YMFL, the common tail.  Line 21 transmits one word
!              from itself to YMFCM (so the message word carries the
!              interrupted address), lines 22-23 call the
!              commentator with the standard "SIC,S COM IC / B,S
!              COMM" pair, lines 24-25 are TWO NULL-OPERATION half
!              words -- the commentator's parameter pair, the
!              message address YMFCM and the decimal count 10 -- and
!              lines 26-27 are "BD,$ / BE,$", a two-way wait whose
!              second half word is YMFIC.
! Lines 29-30  YMFCM, the message itself, in 89-character-set IQS
!              code: "INTERRUPT. THE NEXT INSTRUCTION IS A BE TO THE
!              INTERRUPTED ADDRESS."
! Line 31      YMFCF, a three-word reservation, "DR(N),(3)".
! Lines 32-47  FOUR more fixups, going to YPREL instead: "SIC,YPREL
!              / B,YPREFX" followed by TWO 32-bit literals of the
!              same name, one in the 48-character set and one in the
!              89-character set -- "(AX)DD(BU,32),...X" then
!              "(IQSX)DD(BU,32),...X".  EKJ, UNRJ, CBJ, OP.
! Line 48      YFXAD, the head of a fifth such group, cut off by the
!              page.  See below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NULL OPERATION ON LINES 24 AND 25 IS A PRINTED FORM, AND IT
! WAS TESTED BEFORE IT WAS BELIEVED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 24 and 25 print, in the STATEMENT column with the operation
! field EMPTY:
!
!     24*  216410.00   216412.00 80        ,YMFCM
!     25*  216410.40   000012.00 80        ,10.
!
! The comma sits in the same character cell as the "B" of line 23's
! "B,SCOMM" and the "(" of line 29's "(IQS$)" -- measured on the
! page's own 10-cpi character grid, not eyeballed -- so the
! operation really is blank.  strap_asm already implements this:
! statement_size/emit_statement's "op == ''" case cites C22-6531
! printed p.7 ("the instruction is compiled as if the missing fields
! contained zeros ... called NULL") and Reference Manual printed
! p.163, and emits "the address-and-index half word every full-word
! format begins with" -- address in bits 0-23, the literal 1000 in
! bits 24-27, the index in 28-31.  That is exactly 0x80 with no
! index, which is what both rows print.  NO assembler change was
! needed and none is proposed.
!
! The idiom is not local to this page.  The volume OCR shows the
! same shape after another commentator call: "221037.00 215470.40 80
! SIC,SCOMIC / 221037.40 215470.10 00 B,SCOMM / 221040.00
! 221050.00 80 ,ZIC01", and the next page's line 1 prints
! "221040.40 ... 87" for a statement indexed by $7 -- an index of 7
! in the low nibble, which is the same field this deck's null
! operation leaves at zero.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 48 IS NOT IN THIS DECK, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 48 is "YFXAD  SIC,YPREL" at 216440.00, printing
! "216457.40 80".  Its paired half-word branch is printed p.132
! line 1 ("216440.40  216446.10 00  B,YPREFX", volume OCR).  A SIC
! and the branch after it are ONE 64-bit instruction, and strap_asm
! enforces that -- correctly; real STRAP read the next card and
! never saw a page break.  Writing line 48 alone makes the WHOLE
! deck fail to assemble, and writing a stub branch after it would
! deposit a word at 216440.40 that this page does not print and that
! printed p.132 owns.  So line 48 is recorded in the listing block
! below and nowhere else.
!
! WHAT IS LOST IS SMALL AND BOUNDED.  Line 48's bits,
! "216457.40 80", are the SAME STATEMENT as lines 32, 36, 40 and 44,
! all four of which this deck checks -- so the pattern is verified
! four times over on this page.  The only thing lost is line 48's
! LOCATION, and that is pinned twice anyway: this deck's counter
! ends at exactly 216440.00, and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p110.strap
! already carries "YFXAD SYN,(8)216440.0".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE IS THE DEFINING PAGE FOR ELEVEN OF printed p.110'S SYNs
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p110.strap SYNs eleven symbols it only
! REFERENCES.  Every one of them is DEFINED here, and every one
! lands on p.110's value to the bit:
!
!     YFXMK   216374.00    p110 "YFXMK  SYN,(8)216374.0"
!     YFXIK   216376.00    p110 "YFXIK  SYN,(8)216376.0"
!     YFXIJ   216400.00    p110 "YFXIJ  SYN,(8)216400.0"
!     YFXEK   216402.00    p110 "YFXEK  SYN,(8)216402.0"
!     YFXCPU  216404.00    p110 "YFXCPU SYN,(8)216404.0"
!     YMFIC   216411.40    p110 "YMFIC  SYN,(8)216411.40"
!     YFXEKJ  216430.00    p110 "YFXEKJ SYN,(8)216430.0"
!     YFXUNR  216432.00    p110 "YFXUNR SYN,(8)216432.0"
!     YFXCBJ  216434.00    p110 "YFXCBJ SYN,(8)216434.0"
!     YFXOP   216436.00    p110 "YFXOP  SYN,(8)216436.0"
!     YFXAD   216440.00    p110 "YFXAD  SYN,(8)216440.0"  (line 48)
!
! That is eleven independent confirmations of a SPELLING, which no
! !CHECK can supply -- listing_oracle checks LOCATIONS and BINARY
! and never label spellings.  printed p.110's own witness for YMFIC
! is "215023.00  216411.40 80  S IT  SIC,YMFIC", and for YFXMK
! "215023.40  216374.04 00  BD,YFXMK".
!
! The three names NOT witnessed off-page are YMFL, YMFCM and YMFCF.
! YMFL is referenced from ten rows ON this page (lines 6,7,9,10,12,
! 13,15,16,18,19) and compiles bit-exactly at every one; YMFCM is
! referenced from lines 21 and 24; YMFCF is referenced from printed
! p.132 line 18, which the volume OCR reads as "216453.00
! 216425.03 10  SX,$1,YMFCF" -- word 216425, which is where this
! page's line 31 puts it.
!
! >>> THE VOLUME OCR MISSPELLS ONE OF THEM, AND THE PAGE SETTLES IT
! AGAINST THE OCR. <<<  Line 44's name OCRs twice as "YFXCP"
! (docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt), never as YFXOP.  Rendered at
! 1200 dpi beside line 40's YFXCBJ, the fourth glyph of line 44 is a
! CLOSED round O and line 40's is an open C with no left stem -- and
! ink dropout can open a closed glyph but never close an open one,
! so the closed one is certainly O.  Three further witnesses agree:
! the entry datum this very group punches is " OP " (lines 46-47),
! "OP" is English for the operation-code fixup, and p.110's deck
! already carries "YFXOP SYN,(8)216436.0".  Line 48's last glyph is
! a D by the same test -- a straight vertical LEFT stem -- and
! printed p.132's own entry datum for it reads "AD".
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin here and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed
! p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Every name this page
! DEFINES is Y-prefixed and none collides with anything in pp.2-98.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  WHAT IS READ AND WHAT IS CONVENTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ALL FOUR ADDRESSES BELOW ARE BACK-DERIVED FROM A PRINTED
! INSTRUCTION, AND A BACK-DERIVED ADDRESS IS PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF
! WORD. <<<  Bit offsets 0-31 all encode identically; only bit 32,
! the half-word select, shows.  Writing ".0" or ".40" is therefore a
! reading of the HALF WORD and a CONVENTION within it, and no !CHECK
! on this page can test the bits inside
! (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE",
! item 1).  Two of the four are LANDED in another deck at the same
! value, which is a real second reading.
!
! SCOMM   215470.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap line 293
!                    ("S COMM  B,MCOMD  -EMERGENCY ENTRY TO
!                    COMMMENTATOR"), which is the DEFINING card.
!                    Line 23 here prints 215470.10 00 and B
!                    contributes .10, so the half word is 215470.00.
!                    THE PAGE SPELLS IT WITHOUT BLANKS ("SCOMM")
!                    where p.116 prints "S COMM"; STRAP ignores
!                    blanks in a name and both compile identically.
SCOMM   SYN, (8)215470.0
! SCOMIC  215470.40  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap line 294
!                    ("S COMIC  VF,0").  Line 22 here prints
!                    215470.40 80 and SIC contributes .00, so the
!                    half word is 215470.40.  Spelled "SCOMIC" here
!                    and "S COM IC" on printed pp.133 and 157 of the
!                    same listing (volume OCR), the same two-ways
!                    spelling p.128 found for S CHAN S.
SCOMIC  SYN, (8)215470.40
! YPREL   216457.40  NEW HERE.  Lines 32, 36, 40, 44 and 48 all
!                    print 216457.40 80.  The volume OCR gives the
!                    DEFINING card on printed p.132: "27* 216457.40
!                    216457.40 80 000000.20 50  YPREL  L(BU),$
!                    -LOAD IDENTIFYING INITIALS".  Not rendered
!                    here; it is an OCR reading of a page nobody has
!                    opened.
YPREL   SYN, (8)216457.40
! YPREFX  216446.00  NEW HERE.  Lines 33, 37, 41 and 45 all print
!                    216446.10 00 and B contributes .10.  The volume
!                    OCR gives the defining card on printed p.132:
!                    "12* 216446.00  215001.04 80  216453.34 02
!                    YPREFX  BB,SL,$+5.0".  Same caveat.
YPREFX  SYN, (8)216446.0
!
