!
! The LOCATION-column asterisk (docs/listing_typography.md 12,
! "RECORDED, NOT EXPLAINED" in decks/mcp_bootstrap_p111.strap)
! appears on lines 4, 21, 30 and 31.  Line 4 is the SLC, line 21 is
! the TI -- printed p.124 saw the same mark on three of its TI rows
! -- and lines 30/31 are the message tail and the DR.  No mark
! changes a compiled bit and none is checked.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BLANKS INSIDE THE DD DATA WERE MEASURED, NOT ESTIMATED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The DD rows print NOTHING in the BINARY OUTPUT column (printed
! pp.21, 37 and 103 do the same), so NO !CHECK can see their
! contents.  Only their LENGTHS are checked, by the location of the
! row after them.  The blank counts were read off the page's own
! 10-cpi character grid: the statement column's cell 0 is at x=3507
! in the 400-dpi render and the pitch is 40.0 px, both fitted
! against line 7's known "B,YMFL".
!
!   line  8   datum cells 13-20, "MK" at 18-19  ->  "     MK "   8 chars
!   line 11   same shape                            "     IK "   8
!   line 14   same shape                            "     IJ "   8
!   line 17   same shape                            "     EK "   8
!   line 20   "CPUS" at 16-19                       "   CPUS "   8
!   line 29   8 blanks then cells 21-59         47 chars
!   line 30   cells 13-46, "$" at 47            34 chars
!   lines 34/35  " EKJ"   lines 38/39  "UNRJ"
!   lines 42     "CBJ "   line 43      " CBJ"
!   lines 46/47  " OP "
!
! At eight bits a character (C28-6129 printed p.16: a missing byte
! size is treated modulo 8, so it is eight) each eight-character
! datum is one word, which is what lines 8/11/14/17/20 spend, and
! each four-character datum is 32 bits, which is what "DD(BU,32)"
! declares.
!
! >>> ONE OF THESE IS PINNED ONLY TO A RANGE, AND IT IS LINE 30. <<<
! Line 29's 47 characters land the counter on 216417.70, which is
! line 30's PRINTED location, so 47 is exact.  Line 30's 34
! characters land it on 216424.10 -- and line 31's DR reserves
! WORDS, so the counter is rounded up to 216425.00, which is line
! 31's printed location.  Any length from 34 through 41 characters
! rounds to the same place.  The reading of 34 is the character-grid
! measurement above and nothing else.  Everything downstream of line
! 31 is unaffected either way.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS AND IS NOT CHECKED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Twenty-six !CHECK rows and thirteen !SYM symbols below.  The
! rows NOT checked are exactly the ones that print no binary:
!   * lines 1-3, comment cards;
!   * line 4, an SLC -- an SLC prints no binary;
!   * lines 8,11,14,17,20,29,30,34,35,38,39,42,43,46,47, the DD
!     character literals;
!   * line 28, the CNOP that compiles nothing;
!   * line 31, "DR(N),(3)".  Its printed "000003.00" is the
!     RESERVATION COUNT in the BINARY OUTPUT column, not storage
!     contents, and nothing is deposited for the oracle to read --
!     the same reason printed pp.84, 109 and 114 give their DRZ rows
!     no !CHECK (decks/mcp_bootstrap_p114.strap, whose line 5 prints
!     the identical "000003.00");
!   * line 48, not assembled -- see above.
!
!SYM   YFXMK    216374.00
!SYM   YFXIK    216376.00
!SYM   YFXIJ    216400.00
!SYM   YFXEK    216402.00
!SYM   YFXCPU   216404.00
!SYM   YMFL     216406.00
!SYM   YMFIC    216411.40
!SYM   YMFCM    216412.00
!SYM   YMFCF    216425.00
!SYM   YFXEKJ   216430.00
!SYM   YFXUNR   216432.00
!SYM   YFXCBJ   216434.00
!SYM   YFXOP    216436.00
!
!CHECK 216373.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 5 CNOP -- the counter arrived on a half word
!CHECK 216374.00 | 216406.00 80 | line 6 YFXMK SIC,YMFL
!CHECK 216374.40 | 216406.10 00 | line 7 B,YMFL
!CHECK 216376.00 | 216406.00 80 | line 9 YFXIK SIC,YMFL
